{
 "intro": "<p>Children's doses are calculated by <b>weight (mg/kg)</b> or, for some drugs (chemotherapy, steroids), by <b>body surface area (m²)</b>, and must <b>never exceed the adult dose</b>. Always write the dose, route, frequency and duration, and check the weight. The doses below are those used in Sudanese hospitals and WHO paediatric guidelines.</p>\n<h2 class=\"s\">Prescribing rules</h2>\n<div class=\"two\">\n<div><ul class=\"b\"><li>Weigh every child · if no scale: weight ≈ (age + 4) × 2 (1–10 yr)</li><li>BSA (m²) = √(height cm × weight kg ÷ 3600)</li><li>Neonates: longer intervals (immature kidneys and liver)</li></ul></div>\n<div><ul class=\"b\"><li>Prefer <b>oral</b> syrups/dispersible tablets when the child can swallow · avoid IM in bleeding disorders and polio</li><li>Avoid in children: <b>aspirin</b> (Reye; except Kawasaki, ARF), <b>tetracyclines</b> &lt; 8 yr, <b>ceftriaxone</b> in jaundiced neonates, codeine</li></ul></div>\n</div>",
